{"page": 7, "text": "In addition to the cash consideration noted above, during the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026, GFL paid $2.2 million and $33.3 million, respectively, in additional consideration related to acquisitions from prior years.\nOn September 1, 2026, GFL acquired 100% of the issued and outstanding common shares of SECURE for total consideration of approximately $5,414.1 million. SECURE is an operator of waste processing, industrial waste disposal and recycling located in Western Canada and North Dakota. Due to the timing of the acquisition relative to the release of these Interim Financial Statements, the initial accounting for the acquisition is provisional. GFL has engaged an independent third-party valuation specialist to assist in determining the fair value of certain of the assets acquired, including identifiable intangible assets and property, plant and equipment. As of September 30, 2026, the initial purchase price allocation is provisional and subject to adjustment during the measurement period. Provisional amounts represent historical carrying value. Adjustment to these provisional amounts may significantly impact the recognized values of intangible assets, goodwill, property and equipment and deferred income tax liabilities.\nGFL finalizes purchase price allocations relating to acquisitions within 12 months of the respective acquisition dates and, as a result, there may be differences between the provisional estimates reflected above and the final acquisition accounting. During the nine months ended September 30, 2026, GFL finalized the purchase price allocations for certain acquisitions resulting in a decrease in net working capital of $4.3 million, an increase in property and equipment of $88.4 million, an increase in intangible assets of $31.8 million, an increase in other long-term liabilities of $28.5 million, an increase in closure and post-closure obligations of $0.3 million, an increase in deferred income tax liabilities of $7.1 million, a decrease in goodwill of $114.4 million and a decrease in accrued contingent consideration of $34.4 million.\nApproximately $92.0 million and $444.6 million of the goodwill acquired during the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026 ($65.8 million and $144.0 million of the goodwill acquired during the three and nine months ended September 30, 2025) is expected to be deductible for tax purposes.\nSince the respective acquisition dates, revenue and income before income taxes of approximately $399.0 million and $49.2 million, respectively, attributable to the 2026 acquisitions, are included in these Interim Financial Statements.\nPro forma results of operations\n"}
{"page": 8, "text": "If the 2026 acquisitions had occurred on January 1, 2026, the unaudited consolidated pro forma revenue and loss before income taxes for the nine months ended September 30, 2026 would have been $6,905.3 million and $186.2 million, respectively. The pro forma results do not purport to be indicative of the results of operations which would have resulted had the acquisitions occurred at the beginning of the year, nor are they necessarily indicative of future operating results.\nInvestments in Associates\nEffective March 1, 2025, GFL completed the divestiture of its Environmental Services line of business (\u201cGFL Environmental Services\u201d). GFL has the option to repurchase the balance of the equity of GFL Environmental Services (the \u201cCall Option\u201d). As at September 30, 2026, the Call Option had a fair value of $95.0 million ($140.0 million as at December 31, 2025).\nAs at September 30, 2026, GFL held investments in associates of $1,714.8 million ($1,690.2 million as at December 31, 2025). GFL has accounted for these investments in associates using the equity method.\nFor the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026, GFL\u2019s share of income (loss) from associates was $17.4 million and $(54.2) million ($3.0 million and $(104.7) million for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2025). For the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026, GFL\u2019s share of total comprehensive income (loss) from associates was $44.3 million and $(40.6) million ($7.8 million and $(129.9) million for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2025).\nF-8\nGFL Environmental Inc. - Notes to the Consolidated Financial Statements\n(In millions of dollars except per share amounts or otherwise stated)\nCertain adjustments were made to the results of GFL Environmental Services for the year ended December 31, 2025, related to measurement period adjustments impacting GFL\u2019s initial investment in the associate. Accordingly, comparative amoun