{"page": 18, "text": "The carrying value of GFL\u2019s financial assets approximate their fair values. The carrying value of GFL\u2019s financial liabilities approximate their fair values with the exception of GFL\u2019s outstanding U.S. dollar secured and unsecured notes (the \u201cNotes\u201d) and 4.375% Bonds. The fair value hierarchy for these instruments are as follows for the periods indicated:\nSeptember 30, 2026\nCarrying Value Fair Value Level 1 Level 2 Level 3\nNotes $ 8,582.5 $ 8,239.6 $ \u2014 $ 8,239.6 $ \u2014\n4.375% Bonds 297.9 289.5 \u2014 289.5 \u2014\nDecember 31, 2025\nCarrying Value Fair Value Level 1 Level 2 Level 3\nNotes $ 5,892.0 $ 5,945.9 $ \u2014 $ 5,945.9 $ \u2014\n4.375% Bonds 287.8 291.2 \u2014 291.2 \u2014\nGFL uses a discounted cash flow model incorporating observable market data, such as foreign currency forward rates, to estimate the fair value of its Notes. Certain leases do not bear interest or bear interest at an amount that is not stated at fair value.\nNet derivative instruments are recorded at fair value and classified within Level 2. The Call Option is measured using an option pricing model which includes inputs such as equity volatility, risk-free rates, and implied credit yields. The Call Option is recorded at fair value and classified within Level 3.\nF-21\nGFL Environmental Inc. - Notes to the Consolidated Financial Statements\n(In millions of dollars except per share amounts or otherwise stated)\nFinancial risk management objectives\nThere were no changes to the financial risk management policies disclosed in the Annual Financial Statements.\nOn June 25, 2026, GFL entered into a cross-currency interest rate swap on the 5.625% 2031 Notes, fixing the interest rate at 4.480% and the foreign exchange rate at 1.4202, expiring on July 1, 2030.\nOn August 28, 2026, GFL entered into a cross-currency interest rate swap on the Term Loan B Facility, fixing the interest rate at 5.009% and the foreign exchange rate at 1.3866, expiring on September 30, 2029.\n15. COMMITMENTS\nLetters of credit\nAs at September 30, 2026, GFL had letters of credit totaling approximately $535.1 million outstanding ($415.4 million as at December 31, 2025), which are not recognized in the Interim Financial Statements. This is inclusive of letters of credit under both the Revolving Credit Facility and EDC Guaranteed LC Facility (defined below). Interest expense in connection with these letters of credit was $1.9 million and $5.3 million for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026 ($1.6 million and $5.2 million for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2025).\nUnder the unsecured demand letter of credit and demand guarantee facility agreement dated as of September 5, 2025 and August 10, 2022 (the \u201cEDC Guaranteed LC Facility\u201d), GFL has access to $250.0 million of letters of credit that are 100% guaranteed by Export Development Canada. As of September 30, 2026, GFL had $187.8 million in outstanding letters of credit under the EDC Guaranteed LC Facility ($140.2 million as at December 31, 2025).\nPerformance bonds\n"}
{"page": 19, "text": "As at September 30, 2026, GFL had issued performance bonds totaling $2,324.1 million ($1,936.4 million as at December 31, 2025).\nCrude oil transportation and storage commitments\nAs at September 30, 2026, GFL had crude oil transportation commitments totaling $561.4 million ($nil as at December 31, 2025). Included in this number are committed crude oil volumes for pipeline throughput at certain pipeline-connected terminals. This amount reflects the total payment that would have to be made should GFL fail to deliver the committed pipeline volumes.\nAs at September 30, 2026, GFL had crude oil storage commitments recognized as onerous contracts totaling $51.0 million ($nil as at December 31, 2025).\nF-22\nGFL Environmental Inc. - Notes to the Consolidated Financial Statements\n(In millions of dollars except per share amounts or otherwise stated)\n16. RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS\nIn connection with Patrick Dovigi\u2019s relocation to the United States, GFL agreed to satisfy any tax obligations arising from the relocation. In 2025, GFL paid $33.5 million in satisfaction of this obligation. This amount is expected to be refunded and has been recognized within other receivables.\nFor the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026, GFL paid $4.2 million and $11.8 million ($3.7 million and $10.6 million for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2025) in aggregate lease payments to related parties.\nFor the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026, GFL entered into transactions with Green Infrastructure Partners Inc. which resulted in revenue of $1.0 million and $2.4 million ($0.9 million and $5.2 million for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2025) and net payables of $0.7 million as at September 30, 2026 ($0.5 million as at December 31, 2025).\nFor the three and nine months ended September 30, 2026, GFL entered into transactions with GFL Environmental Services which resulted in revenue of $11.6 million and $29.1 million ($8.1 million and $20.8 million for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2025), deferred revenue of $51.2 million as at September 30, 2026 ($62.6 million as at December 31, 2025) and net payables of $13.7 million as at September 30, 2026 ($43.7 million as at December 31, 2025).\n17. DISCONTINUED OPERATIONS\nThe results of GFL Environmental Services are presented as a single amount on the statement of operations and comprehensive income (loss). The post-tax results of the discontinued operations for the periods indicated are as follows:\nThree months ended\nSeptember 30, Nine months ended\nSeptember 30,\n2026 2025 2026 2025\nRevenue $ \u2014 $ \u2014 $ \u2014 $ 237.0\nExpenses \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 209.1\nIncome before income taxes \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 27.9\nIncome tax expense \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 0.6\nNet income \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 27.3\nGain on disposal \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 4,466.8\nIncome tax on gain on disposal \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 873.3\nNet income from discontinued operations \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 3,620.8\nReclassification to net income of foreign currency translation adjustment on divestiture \u2014 \u2014 \u2014 (176.5 )\n"}
